    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d381">

                <pb facs="0423" n="389" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg389"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sherman to Mr.
                            Romero.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-03-10"><hi rendition="#italic">March 10,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 227.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In connection with the Department’s note of
                    the 5th instant in reply to yours of the 1st, stating that certain Indians of
                    the Fort Yuma Reservation in California have crossed over into Mexican territory
                    and have established themselves on the ranch of Mr. Guillermo Andrade, I have
                    the honor to inform you that the Department is now in receipt of a letter from
                    the Secretary of the Interior, of the 6th instant, stating that the matter has
                    been referred to the Commissioner of Indian Affairs for immediate consideration
                    and report.</p>
                <p>Upon the receipt of a statement of the result of the investigation I shall take
                    pleasure in duly advising you thereof.</p>
                <p>Accept, Mr. Minister, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Sherman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
